# In a build of a program the link is allocated where its constructor ends, with every field. Where proofs are checked the first allocation stays, and what a second would be born with is asked of it: a checked build makes no more links than another.
# f1 = push, f3 = Link
# OPTIONS: testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RUN: walk f1
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[made]]: L0 @Cell = NewObject layout=L0
# CHECK: = GetSlot [[made]] key="left"
# CHECK: CheckProof
# CHECK: = GetSlot [[made]] key="id"
# CHECK: CheckProof
# CHECK: = GetSlot [[made]] key="next"
# CHECK: CheckProof
# RUN(ONCE): walk f1
# ONCE-COUNT-1: = NewObject
# ONCE-NOT: = NewObject
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: b5null
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
